# Circle · visual references

- Stamen’s Watercolor suggests translucent pigment for the Field Guide’s neighbourhood boundaries. [Watercolor process](https://stamen.com/watercolor-process-3dd5135861fe/)
- Giorgia Lupi and Stefanie Posavec’s postcard legends suggest using repeated ink marks to show room activity. [Dear Data](https://www.dear-data.com/theproject)
- Stamen’s Toner suggests a restrained street network that lets the Night Signal activity layer stand out. [Toner, Terrain and Watercolor](https://stamen.com/maps-stamen-com-is-live-4e4dde30dd72/)
- Pentagram’s Public Theater identity suggests a tightly set, high-impact headline for the Block Press. [The Public Theater](https://www.pentagram.com/work/the-public-theater)
- The Rumsey map collection suggests treating the city name, compass and map margin as parts of the same printed sheet. [David Rumsey Map Collection](https://www.davidrumsey.com/)
EOF
